message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "RDSI: The Hidden Mathematics Behind the Clock"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
abstract: >
  The RDSI repository accompanies a series of papers on linear Diophantine
  representation systems with the foundation relation p ≡ 1 (mod q).
  It compares two structurally opposite architectures that share the same
  equation shape: the (25,12) system N = 25A + 12B, which produces an
  ordered ladder of representations and whose smallest coefficient is
  A₀ = N mod 12 in a single step, and the clock [3600,60,1], which
  guarantees exactly one representation per instant through a hierarchical
  divisibility chain with bounded coefficients. The papers formalise the
  choice between 0-based and 1-based cycle models, prove that positional
  divisibility and the modular condition are structurally incompatible,
  and measure the difference in software: a 0-based model needs six
  conditional branches to be correct at every boundary, while a 1-based
  model p ≡ 1 (mod q) needs none. The repository ships the reference
  implementation (rd, Representation Domain) with a branch-free core,
  enforced by CI, and an interactive demo.
type: software
